# Civil War Strategy: menus of the Commands menu that the player gives up with Esc, and
# Fortify with no city left. The game is loaded from a prepared save
# (tests/data/given-up/cws1.save): May 1862, the Rebels play, with 1000 in cash and two
# armies, both in Richmond. The computer is passive.
# A message shows on the bottom line under the next menu.
#! seed 6
#! cfg side=2 bold=0
#! data given-up

rule 1 key space

# The title menu: Resume Saved Game; the Load menu: the one save.
play until 2:C
text r
play until 2:L
key enter
play until 2:M
digest

# COMMANDS, Fortify: one row, Richmond, though two armies are there. Esc gives it up: the Commands menu again,
# on Fortify, since the Rebels can still pay for a fort.
text c
prompt
text f
prompt
digest
key esc
prompt
digest

# Fortify, Richmond: its fort grows a level, and the Commands menu comes back on Fortify.
key enter
prompt
key enter
prompt
digest

# Fortify, Richmond again: the second level in the same month. The army made busy is the
# first in the city both times, so an army that has acted may fortify.
key enter
prompt
key enter
prompt
digest

# Fortify a third time: Richmond's fort is at its limit, so "No cities eligible to fortify",
# and the Commands menu again.
key enter
prompt
digest

# Three rows down to Capital: the picker shows Richmond. Esc gives it up: the 500 stays paid,
# and the main menu comes back.
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
prompt
digest
key esc
prompt
digest

# Files, Quit, Yes, and a key for END's "Press any key to continue".
text f
prompt
text q
prompt
text y
repeat space
